+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is handed verbatim to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates incoming model arguments against that schema before the tool's executor runs. Rejecting malformed input as a `ToolResponse` rather than a thrown exception feeds the failure back into the `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` tool loop so the model can correct its call within the round budget instead of aborting the turn.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the executor, returning a `ToolResponse` that names the failing property path and constraint while never exposing input field values in either the returned `result` or emitted log lines ([validated by: rejects wrong-typed input without running executor or leaking values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L13)).
+- Registering a static `ToolDefinition` compiles its `inputSchema` during `register` and throws immediately, naming the tool, when the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws naming the tool when registering an uncompilable static schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L62)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves and validates against the schema returned at each `execute` call, enforcing `required`, declared types, and `enum` while passing valid input and unlisted extra properties through untouched without type coercion or applied defaults ([validated by: validates against dynamic schemas while preserving extra input keys](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L80)).
+- Missing `required` fields and other schema violations return a `ToolResponse` rather than throwing, so `ChatOrchestrator` feeds the rejection text back to the provider as a `tool_result` message and resolves once the model retries within the round budget ([validated by: returns missing-required rejections in the tool loop so retries resolve](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L118)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled once at registration rather than recompiled on every `execute` call, and a function-valued definition caches compiled validators by the resolved schema object.
+- Calling `ToolRegistry.execute` with an unregistered tool name continues to throw `Unknown tool: <name>` rather than returning a `ToolResponse`.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Converting `Unknown tool: <name>` from a thrown `Error` to a returned `ToolResponse` is tracked separately because changing it alters direct caller behaviour.
+- Validating tool output, per-tool authorization against `ToolContext`, and retry, timeout, or rate limiting around tool execution remain outside this contract.
